Ver1.7
  - sleep-power-control: keyboard sleep signal. Before detaching the keyboard the
    service sets one bit (default: Kana) in the keyboard's HID LED output report and
    clears it after re-attach; the layout is read from the report descriptor. Firmware
    that understands it (uConsole-tweaks/zmk-uc9900 on the bb9900) darkens the key
    backlight and trackpad light and parks itself. KB_SLEEP_LED / KB_SLEEP_LED_WAIT_SEC.
    New helper src/kb_hid_led.py, also a CLI for manual testing.
  - sleep-power-control: optional USB suspend of the keyboard after the driver unbind,
    KB_SLEEP_USB_SUSPEND, default no: on the uConsole hub the bb9900 suspends but does
    not resume (runtime_status=error, "can't set config #1, error -22" on rebind)
  - sleep-power-control: keyboard sleep is deferred by KB_SLEEP_DELAY_SEC (1s) and
    cancelled if the screen comes back, so sleep-idle-alert's backlight flash wakes the
    keyboard once instead of detaching/re-attaching it on every pulse
  - sleep-power-control: skip bind/unbind when the keyboard is already in that state
    (removes the "[Errno 16] Device or resource busy" journal noise at startup)
  - sleep-power-control: optional sleep-time knobs, off by default, applied with the
    deferred keyboard sleep and reverted on wake: SLEEP_WIFI_POWERSAVE (iw power save,
    link stays up), SLEEP_BT_OFF (rfkill block when nothing is connected), SLEEP_CPU_QUOTA
    (runtime systemd CPUQuota on user slices). New src/sleep_knobs.py; `iw` dependency.
    Ships a polkit rule allowing org.blueman.rfkill.setstate for active local sessions
    so the blueman applet does not prompt for a password when Bluetooth is blocked.
  - sleep-remap-powerkey: POWERKEY_DPMS_OFF_CMD / POWERKEY_DPMS_ON_CMD run the
    compositor's DPMS command as the logged-in user around the power-key sleep/wake
    (session env discovered from the compositor process; new src/user_session.py).
    Without it Hyprland keeps scanning out to the dark panel, ~0.7 W on a CM5 uConsole.
  - Makefile: VERSION 1.7

Ver1.6
  - new sleep-idle-alert user service: cross-DE post-idle escalator with audio tiers and backlight flash
  - X11 idle detection via python3-xlib; Wayland via swayidle subprocess
  - on-battery anchored squawk ladder (gentle -> nag -> dumbass); plugging in or activity resets the ladder
  - per-tier curated filename lists via IDLE_SOUNDS_<TIER> (pipe-separated) take priority over
    tier subdirs and flat IDLE_SOUND_DIR; ships with the prior IdleAlert.sh per-device curation as defaults
  - falls back to sound-theme-freedesktop for built-in sounds when nothing else resolves
  - shipped udev rule grants the video group write on /sys/class/backlight/*/bl_power
  - sleep-idle-alert: optional DPMS wake/sleep around each flash via IDLE_DPMS_WAKE_CMD /
    IDLE_DPMS_SLEEP_CMD (+ IDLE_DPMS_WAKE_SETTLE_SEC), so backlight pulses stay visible when
    the compositor has DPMS-off'd the panel; both default empty to preserve prior behavior.
    config.default ships Hyprland / sway / X11 examples
  - keyboard detection: add ZMK bb9900 (1d50:615e) to the built-in keyboard VID:PID allowlist
    in find_internal_kb.py
  - idle alerter is optional at build time: `make WITH_IDLE_ALERTER=0 build` skips the script,
    user unit, udev rule, and python3-xlib/swayidle/sound-theme-freedesktop dependencies
  - sleep-idle-alert unit: WantedBy=default.target so it auto-starts on user
    login regardless of whether the compositor pulls graphical-session.target up
    (KDE/GNOME do; Hyprland/labwc/openbox typically don't); restart backoff
    (RestartSec=10s, StartLimitBurst=5/5min)
  - sleep-idle-alert: flash now restores the pre-flash bl_power value so the
    pulse train no longer leaves a lit screen blanked (the bash original was
    fine ending dark because it only ran during DPMS-off + hyprlock; the
    Python port has neither gate, so it must restore state)
  - Makefile: new user-status / user-logs targets; VERSION 1.6

Ver1.5
  - sleep-power-control: skip CPU freq clamp when on AC, with 30s AC poll while screen is off
  - new sleep-cpu-governor service: drops to `powersave` below 20% battery, restores `schedutil` at >=25% (with hysteresis)
  - add Makefile wrapping build/install/clean/status/logs targets

Ver1.4
  - drop usage of `pyinstaller` (services are now shell wrappers, not compiled binaries)
  - replace inotify simple with inotify
  - source files extracted to `src/` - no longer inlined as heredocs
  - no need to build package as `root`
  - translate Korean to English in error message 
  - improve documentation
  - fixed logging (now the print statements appear in journal)
  - add CHANGES file

Ver1.3
  - autodetect path to power key

Ver1.2
  - Add customization (`/etc/uconsole-sleep/config`)
  - Power saving CPU freq now follows a user-specified value, not available value.

Ver1.1
